You are a senior full-stack engineer building "AuraEngine — Competitor Aura Steal" for a hackathon track: CONTENT MACHINE.

Read PROJECT_SPEC.md before writing code. It is the team contract.

Tech Stack:
- Frontend: Next.js (App Router), Tailwind CSS, Lucide Icons, Framer Motion
- Backend & Realtime State: Convex (Mutations, Queries, Actions, HTTP Actions)
- Auth: Convex Auth (email/password + Google)
- External APIs: OpenAI (GPT-4o), ElevenLabs (TTS), Apify / Exa, fal.ai

Team file ownership — do not edit files outside your column without asking:
- Jordi: src/components/ui/*, design tokens, AuraCounter, RiskSlider
- Josue: convex/schema.ts, convex/brands.ts, convex/preferences.ts, convex/authz.ts, convex/domain.ts
- Deyane: convex/analysis.ts, convex/assets.ts, convex/lib/*, all external API calls in actions
- Hugo / Hector: convex/publisher.ts, convex/social.ts, app routes, Convex client wiring

Rules:
1. Adhere strictly to official Convex patterns: define schemas in convex/schema.ts, keep database logic in mutations/queries, keep external API calls in actions.
2. Every query/mutation that takes a brandId must verify the brand belongs to the authenticated user via requireBrandOwner.
3. OAuth tokens never leave the backend. listConnected strips accessToken/refreshToken.
4. No hard deletes — archive or status transitions only.
5. Build responsive, cyberpunk/dark-mode aesthetic UI components with Tailwind CSS.
6. Every component must be production-grade, typed with TypeScript interfaces, with no mock placeholders unless explicitly marked TODO.
7. Keep components modular and isolated to prevent merge conflicts across the team.
8. Everything hangs off brandId. Preferences live on the brand, not the user.
